# spec_id: eravos.wub-rate · version 1.0.0 · status built · template eravos.tool/1
identity:
  id: eravos.wub-rate ; label: Wub Rate ; domain: music ; category: wubs (shown as Wubs)
  purpose: the rhythm of a wobble — a step pattern of wobble rates; its output opens whatever it is wired to.
ports:
  in:  transport (ticks, play, stop) · mod.depth (±1 → ±1 on the output level) ·
       note:trigger to any Wub Osc (observed, not wired: restarts the wobble when Notes restart is on)
  out: out (modulation) — wire to Wub Filter's "wub", or any violet input
params: steps (16 × [off, hold, 1/1, 1/2, 1/4, 1/4t, 1/8, 1/8t, 1/16, 1/16t, 1/32], hidden) · length 1..16 ·
  stepLen [1/16, 1/8, 1/4, 1/2, 1/1] · shape [sine, talk, sawdown, sawup, square, triangle] · phase 0..1 ·
  smooth 0..1 · polarity [unipolar+, unipolar−, bipolar, bipolar inverted] · depth 0..1 ·
  retrig [on change, every step, never] · noteRetrig
behaviour:
  - shapes are drawn so −1 = closed, +1 = open; phase 0 = where a restarted wobble begins
  - polarity maps the shape x to c + k·x: unipolar+ 0→1 · unipolar− 0→−1 · bipolar −1→1 · bipolar inverted 1→−1
  - output = depth · (c + k·x), then a one-pole-ish low-pass (Smooth: Nyquist → 6 Hz) so hard edges don't click
  - on every transport 16th that starts a step (stepLen), step = (song step ÷ stepLen) mod length, applied at the
    tick's audio time: a rate restarts the wobble from closed (on change: only when the rate differs; every step:
    always; never: the rate changes in place) · hold keeps going · off holds the closed value until the next rate
  - a restart stops every still-scheduled oscillator at that time, so overlapping restarts never double up
  - stopped transport: runs free at the first playable rate, so the wobble is heard while it is shaped
  - BPM changes retune the running wobble at the next tick
  - ui: step_set {index, value} · steps_set {steps} · steps_shift {by}; the window lights the playing step
packs: ships [factory] — 10 patterns: Classic 1/8 · Half-time Talk · Triplet Roll · Brostep Switch-up · Riddim Stabs ·
  Slow Yoi 1/2 · Saw Down Chops · Rising Saw Build · Bipolar Swirl 1/4 · Sub Pump (to Wub Sub level)
acceptance (wub-rate.test.js): the tool contract · free run at 1/8 and 120 BPM cycles at 4 Hz · unipolar+ stays in
  0..1, bipolar reaches both signs, inverted flips · steps follow the transport (a 1/4 step then a 1/16 step change the
  cycle rate at the step boundary) · off holds closed · step_set rejects a bad value

# ---- dependencies (generated by build/specs.mjs — do not edit by hand)
dependencies:
  mode: music   # Music Production
  toolbar_units: [music.engine, music.transport, music.tempo]   # ui expansion when added: Audio engine · Transport · Tempo
  services:
    - audio: Audio engine — shares the audio clock
    - clock: Master clock & tempo — locks to the beat
    - mod: 1 modulation input — LFO / XY / Macro can move them
  inputs:
    - wubrate.hook.transport_in (transport:tick|transport:play|transport:stop) — ambient broadcast
    - wubrate.hook.mod_depth (modulation · port mod.depth)
  outputs:
    - wubrate.hook.mod_out (modulation · port out)
  permissions: [audio_out, bus_publish, bus_subscribe, registry_read]
  works_with: []

